This function is a single comparison, so there is nothing meaningful to speed up. The rewrite makes the conversion to `FIT_BOOL` explicit and compiles to the same code. It returns the same value for every input, so behavior is unchanged.

```cpp
FIT_BOOL Field::IsValid(void) const
{
    return static_cast<FIT_BOOL>(profileIndex != static_cast<FIT_UINT16>(FIT_UINT16_INVALID));
}
```